content:
I'll begin by exploring the workspace and understanding the data structure. Let me start by listing files and reading the data. ```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Let me read the data file to understand its structure: ```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/incident_narratives.csv"
  }
}
```

Now I understand the data. I have 6 incidents with EDR and network IDS sources. Let me create the necessary directories and start building the analysis pipeline. ```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir -p code outputs report/images"
  }
}
```

Let me use Windows-compatible commands: ```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "if not exist code mkdir code && if not exist outputs mkdir outputs && if not exist report mkdir report && if not exist report\\images mkdir report\\images"
  }
}
```

Let me run the preprocessing script: ```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python preprocessing.py"
  }
}
```

Let me run the Gemini triage script: ```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python gemini_triage.py"
  }
}
```

Let me run the visualization script: ```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python visualizations.py"
  }
}
```

Let me verify all deliverables are in place: ```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir /s /b code outputs report"
  }
}
```

Let me verify the gemini_raw.json file content: ```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "outputs/gemini_raw.json"
  }
}
```
